  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Community-Led and Survivor-Centred Approaches to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence and Femicide (GBVF) in South Africa.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is in support of the UN Women 16 Days of Activism activity which seeks to reaffirm commitments to peace and justice, and to elevate citizen participation in shaping South Africa&#x2019;s peace and security agenda.

The activity will, 
- Position &#x201c;16+ Voices on Peace&#x201d; as a national resource for reflection, awareness, and advocacy.
-  Honour the intersection of WPS, YPS, and GBVF activism.
- Mobilise communities and partners to advance GBVF prevention and peacebuilding.
- Amplify diverse lived experiences and community wisdom on peace.
- Strengthen intergenerational dialogue on peace, justice, and safety.</narrative>
  </description>
